From 101fa05d5f26175d2bc8adf939105e334808c6ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:05:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: swigluoai FFN epilogues, pointwise kernel
 and router (T4)

Adds act_mode 2/3 (swigluoai: gate clamped above, or both sides; alpha, limit and
the "+1" are kernel arguments, not constants) to the grouped-expert and EXL3
epilogues: exl3_experts.cu (decode gateup epilogue, plan_finish, prompt_gu),
x3gm/x3gm2/x3gm3 and x3ld_epi. act_mode 0/1 take the same code as before.
minimax_m3_act.cu holds the pointwise swigluoai for the dense layers and the
shared expert, and tf_mm3_route_warp, a router ranking by sigmoid(logit) + bias
(moe_glue's tf_moe_topk_sigmoid ranks by logit + bias, which differs once the
correction bias is non-zero).

Zig: exl3_experts.Layer.act_mode/alpha/up_bias, Stage and launch plumbing,
exl3_block Act/Epi/GmArgs fields, cuda/minimax_m3_act.zig, families/minimax_m3/ffn.zig
(switch -> argument mapping, route plan), registry records, a contract test with
float64 reference and two planted controls. Nothing here has run on a GPU.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
